    <h1>Sel Roti Recipe</h1>

    <p>
        <strong>Sel Roti</strong> is a traditional Nepali rice bread that is
        crispy on the outside and soft on the inside. It is especially popular
        during festivals and celebrations.
    </p>

    <img
    src="https://www.willflyforfood.net/wp-content/uploads/2022/05/donuts-sel-roti.jpg"
    alt="Traditional Nepali Sel Roti"
    width="300"
    height="200"
>

    <h2>Ingredients</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Rice</li>
        <li>Sugar</li>
        <li>Milk</li>
        <li>Ghee</li>
        <li>Cardamom</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Preparation</h2>

    <ol>
        <li>Soak the rice overnight and grind it into a smooth batter.</li>
        <li>Add sugar, milk, ghee, and cardamom to the batter.</li>
        <li>Mix everything until the batter is smooth.</li>
        <li>Heat oil in a deep pan.</li>
        <li>Pour the batter into the oil in a ring shape.</li>
        <li>Fry until golden brown and serve.</li>
    </ol>

